{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition","id":1195842,"title":"Need some help with using Auspex with 2nd edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-15T14:14:37-07:00","id":1195842,"title":"Need some help with using Auspex with 2nd edition","content":"So I am new to 2nd edition and I have looked over the Auspex powers. We are starting more powerful so I do have 5 dots in Auspex. Can I have some suggestions or advice on the most effective ways to use Auspex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T14:38:02-07:00","id":1195851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition#post1195842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am new to 2nd edition and I have looked over the Auspex powers. We are starting more powerful so I do have 5 dots in Auspex. Can I have some suggestions or advice on the most effective ways to use Auspex?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works pretty much the same as it did in 1st Edition. Dot by dot, some noteworthy changes to keep in mind are:<br /> <br /> \u2022: This is the only power that\u2019s totally different from 1e. Think of this like a Aura Reading, but only surface level, and for the scene as a whole rather than an individual. So you can check if the scene is tense of relaxed, what\u2019s the most likely source of danger, that kind of thing. What\u2019s nice is that the first use in the scene is free, so you can start off every scene with a quick scan to see if anyone wants to hurt you or whatever. Very nice.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022: The Q&amp;A format makes it look more different than it is, but practically speaking, it\u2019s the same power. Instead of getting Aura colors, you get sensory descriptions, but you still use it the same way otherwise. Scan people and see what their emotional state is, if they\u2019re a vampire, if they\u2019re stained by diablerie, etc. Again, the first use against each person in a scene is free, so there\u2019s no reason not to start of every interaction with a quick scan for their emotional state, if they\u2019re hiding something from you, etc.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Again, basically the same power as Spirit\u2019s Touch, only now instead of getting a vision mostly determined by the ST, you have a little more say in what you learn about the object in the form of the Q&amp;A.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: This is still basically telepathy. The nice thing is that the ability to assault someone\u2019s mind with it is a bit better codified now. Use it to have private conversations that can\u2019t be listened in on, to read people\u2019s minds, or to give people horrifying visions just like before, now with the added benefit of knowing exactly what Condition they\u2019ll get if you do the latter. Free to initiate telepathic contact, 1 vitae per memory viewed or projected.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: This really has no practical change from 1st Edition. The biggest thing to keep in mind is that other vampires can sense your projection with only Auspex 1, if they think to ask about it. So it\u2019s a little less effective at infiltration if there are vampires in the place you\u2019re infiltrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:43:25-07:00","id":1195898,"title":"","content":"As mentioned, with 1-2, using them their free time is something you may as well get into a habit of.<br /> <br /> With 3, another thing to mention that couldn't be done in 1e is that you can use it on *locations* too. For Ordo (and to a lesser extent, Circle/Lance), being able to ask if it's a &quot;Supernatural Location&quot; is great for discovering Nests. Not sure what your covenant is though.<br /> <br /> If you can reliably get exceptional successes on level 4, it can become a fairly large buff/debuff ability. Grant a bunch of Inspired, Steadfast, etc, or by contrast inflict with spooked, guilty, etc; each of those free memories is another condition you can inflict if you don't want to be secretive about what you're doing.<br /> <br /> (As a note, AUspex 1 could sense Auspex 5 in 1e too, and since you blatantly need to ASK now instead of just popping heightened senses, you're actually much safer since, in my experience at least, few mekhet will randomly check for psychic projections in every scene)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 03-19-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T02:25:52-07:00","id":1196000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition?p=1195851#post1195851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022\u2022: The Q&amp;A format makes it look more different than it is, but practically speaking, it\u2019s the same power. Instead of getting Aura colors, you get sensory descriptions, but you still use it the same way otherwise. Scan people and see what their emotional state is, if they\u2019re a vampire, if they\u2019re stained by diablerie, etc. Again, the first use against each person in a scene is free, so there\u2019s no reason not to start of every interaction with a quick scan for their emotional state, if they\u2019re hiding something from you, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of Auspex 2 was one free use per scene not one free use on each individual per scene.<br /> When I was playing a Mekhet I made a point of using my free uses of Auspex any time I didn't think a better option would come up in the scene and when in doubt what question to ask I checked if they were a diablerist. Getting the perfect use is probably less useful than using it lots and building up your understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T06:59:29-07:00","id":1196038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition?p=1196000#post1196000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My reading of Auspex 2 was one free use per scene not one free use on each individual per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the wording in the book is \u201cCost: Varies; the first use in a scene is free, but subsequent uses <b>against the same target</b> that scene cost 1 Vitae each.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:59:54-07:00","id":1196061,"title":"","content":"Note, since you're playing in my game, I am emphasizing the &quot;failed powers create a small visible effect&quot;, and I'm allowing a Wits+Occult-2 roll to notice them, so some of those powers are not a completely free/safe way to get info. If you fail - someone might notice that someone is using powers. And if there's only two of you there... <br /> <br /> Other than that, what others said is largely true","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T10:55:39-07:00","id":1196126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition?p=1196038#post1196038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the wording in the book is \u201cCost: Varies; the first use in a scene is free, but subsequent uses <b>against the same target</b> that scene cost 1 Vitae each.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed that, Mekhet are better than I gave them credit for and they were already my favourite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T10:59:33-07:00","id":1196128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition?p=1196061#post1196061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, since you're playing in my game, I am emphasizing the &quot;failed powers create a small visible effect&quot;, and I'm allowing a Wits+Occult-2 roll to notice them, so some of those powers are not a completely free/safe way to get info. If you fail - someone might notice that someone is using powers. And if there's only two of you there... <br /> <br /> Other than that, what others said is largely true</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a your homebrew? Because if I'm not wrong in the Auspex description is stated it is absolutely impossible to notice someone is using the power. But I could remember wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T11:36:04-07:00","id":1196146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition?p=1196128#post1196128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a your homebrew? Because if I'm not wrong in the Auspex description is stated it is absolutely impossible to notice someone is using the power. But I could remember wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Other vampires have no way to know when someone is using Auspex to discover their secrets&quot; doesn't really contradict this general facet of Using Disciplines:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each Discipline calls on the Beast, whether using its talents overtly or expressing it through the blood inside. While the mechanical effect of a player failing her Discipline roll is that nothing happens, that\u2019s not strictly true. Something happens. The Beast won\u2019t just accept the idea that tapping its power produces no results. Maybe the lights flicker, or the vampire\u2019s flesh writhes on her bones for just a second. Maybe her victim sees a second, screaming face trying to escape the vampire\u2019s head for just a second. Whatever it is, it\u2019s not enough to properly freak her victim out \u2014 that\u2019s the domain of the Nosferatu, through their Nightmare Discipline. It\u2019s just something that reminds the vampire that she\u2019s not human, she\u2019s tapping something within herself that she doesn\u2019t fully understand and cannot truly control. The Storyteller and player should work together to come up with a couple of potential minor signs that the vampire\u2019s tried to use a Discipline, even though nothing particularly supernatural has happened. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T13:17:07-07:00","id":1196576,"title":"","content":"Pretty much what Satchel said. If you succeed on Auspex - that doesn't happen and the only way to learn about it is another user of Auspex.<br /> I just gave that fluffy description a little bit more mechanics to go alongside it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:48:23-07:00","id":1197216,"title":"","content":"Yes, in Griautis's game I tried to Lay Open the Mind on the Prince - I failed and the lights flickered. The Prince mentioned it, but he just warned me (probably because this was my first scene in the game). However, I did use Uncanny Perception on him and found out he is a diablerist (no big surprise there). I am fine with the Wits + Occult -2 check to notice, it makes sense. Auspex is one of my favorite disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T14:01:24-07:00","id":1197735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1195842-need-some-help-with-using-auspex-with-2nd-edition?p=1197216#post1197216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in Griautis's game I tried to Lay Open the Mind on the Prince - I failed and the lights flickered. The Prince mentioned it, but he just warned me (probably because this was my first scene in the game). However, I did use Uncanny Perception on him and found out he is a diablerist (no big surprise there). I am fine with the Wits + Occult -2 check to notice, it makes sense. Auspex is one of my favorite disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right, I didn't want to fuck up your relationship with the Prince from the get go, just because you didn't know there was a chance for him to notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}